 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 241178,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/85aacdd541788482.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Rafael Sanjuán, et al./<i>Journal of Virology</i>)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the mutation rates of different viruses and bacteria. The ss stands for single strand, ds for double strand, and retro for retroviruses (RNA viruses which transcribe DNA and add it to host's DNA).</p>\n<p>The SARS-CoV-2 virus that caused the 2020 pandemic is a single stranded RNA virus with positive polarity (ss+RNA). Its mutation rate is comparatively low, when considering ss(+)RNA viruses.</p>\n<p>Based on the patterns you see in the graph, make a prediction about the genome size of the SARS-CoV-2.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 754176,
     "content_html": "It has a genome size between 100 and 1,000 nt, most likely closer to 1,000 nt."
    },
    {
     "id": 754175,
     "content_html": "It has a genome size between between 1,000 and 10,000 nt, most likely around 5,000 nt."
    },
    {
     "id": 754174,
     "content_html": "It has a genome size between slightly below 10,000 nt."
    },
    {
     "id": 754177,
     "content_html": "It has a genome size between above 10,000 nt."
    }
   ],
